  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rehabilitation of a High School Teacher&apos;s Training Center in the Republic of Palau</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">School infrastructure in Palau is exposed to several hazardous conditions which will likely to become more severe with the increasing impact of climate change.  High winds can cause damage to roof coverings and lightweight structures.  Salty and humid atmosphere can cause significant decay to building materials.  Coastal locations can result in exposure to storm surge flooding.  High heat and humidity can also lead to material degradation as well as undermining the learning environment.</narrative>
  </description>
